cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ProofZero
message: >-
  If you use this repository, its notes, or its bounded verification
  tools, please cite it as software. Please do not cite it as a result.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ProofZero contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thabs1234/proofzero"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A collection of research notes on ten open mathematical problems: the six
  open Clay Millennium Prize Problems, the Poincare Conjecture as a solved
  historical control, and three classic conjectures (Collatz, Goldbach,
  twin primes). Each note separates what is known, what can be checked
  here, and where the open edge lies. The tools give finite evidence on
  small bounds and nothing more. No proof is claimed, and none of the ten
  problems is resolved by anything in this repository.


  Please cite published bounds where they are cited -- Oliveira e Silva,
  Herzog and Pardi for Goldbach to 4e18; Barina for Collatz to 2^68;
  Platt and Trudgian for Riemann zeros to 3e12; Zhang, Maynard and Tao for
  bounded prime gaps. This repository reproduces none of them.
keywords:
  - mathematics
  - open problems
  - computational verification
  - reproducible research
  - research notes
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
references:
  - type: standard
    title: >-
      Note on citation scope: this repository is a literature and tooling
      resource. Citing it acknowledges the notes and tools, not any
      mathematical claim. Finite computations in tools/ establish
      nothing about any conjecture's general case, and the four Millennium
      problems with no tool (Navier-Stokes, Yang-Mills, Birch and
      Swinnerton-Dyer, Hodge) have none because no honest finite check
      for them exists here.
